From: guille-vega <guillermo.vega@balena.io>
Subject: spl: imx: Delay before panic on FIT FDT authentication failure

With CONFIG_IMX_SPL_FIT_FDT_SIGNATURE the SPL authenticates the FIT FDT
before the FIT images, and panics right away when that fails. The board
resets before the ethernet link comes up, which the bootloader integrity
tests monitor as the signal that the device has powered up.

Delay before that panic too, as it is done for the FIT images.

Signed-off-by: guille-vega <guillermo.vega@balena.io>

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [balena bootloader integrity tests only]
---
 arch/arm/mach-imx/spl.c | 3 +++
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm/mach-imx/spl.c b/arch/arm/mach-imx/spl.c
--- a/arch/arm/mach-imx/spl.c
+++ b/arch/arm/mach-imx/spl.c
@@ -414,6 +414,9 @@
 				printf("spl: ERROR:  FIT FDT authentication unsuccessful\n");
 				return NULL;
 #else
+				/* Give time for ethernet to come up before panic */
+				/* to signal device has booted and use it in tests  */
+				mdelay(3000);
 				panic("spl: ERROR:  FIT FDT authentication unsuccessful\n");
 #endif
 			}
